<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banda Singh Bahadur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1670">1670</a>–<a href="/years/1716">1716</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banda Singh Bahadur was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> military leader who, after meeting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guru-gobind-singh">Guru Gobind Singh</a> in 1708, led a rising against Mughal rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>. He captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirhind">Sirhind</a> in 1710, set up a Sikh administration with its own coinage and abolished the zamindari estates in the areas he held. Besieged and captured at Gurdas Nangal, he was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1716.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banda-singh-bahadur.jpg" alt="Banda Singh Bahadur" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Possible_depiction_of_Banda_Singh_Bahadur_from_an_illustrated_folio_of_%E2%80%98Tawarikh-i_Jahandar_Shah%E2%80%99,_Awadh_or_Lucknow,_ca.1770.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
